 "script": "studies/campaign/runs/training-land-weighted-2026-11-22/evaluations/game_size.py",
 "method": "How large a game of the campaign is, decision by decision, for sizing the network and the search.\n\nThe owner asked on 24 November 2026 for the network and the search to be sized from AlphaZero's and KataGo's, by\ncomparing this game with theirs. This replays, without searching, the move logs of self-play games of the training\nrun under the land-weighted score that collect_finished_games.sh kept (self-play-moves-update-363/ and\nself-play-moves-update-595/, each game copied at most 10 seconds before its end), and records at every decision the\nnumber of legal actions, the nation whose turn it is, the phase and the game round, and counts the chance events.\nFrom these it works out: decisions a game; the legal actions a decision (mean, median, percentiles); the sum of\nlog10(legal actions) over a game's decisions, the size of the tree of a game's action sequences leaving the dice\nout, as Shannon's 10^120 for chess counts it; decisions a Player Turn and a phase; and the same by phase. Run from\nthe run's code folder with PYTHONPATH set to it:  game_size.py OUTPUT FOLDER [FOLDER ...]\nThe replayed decisions are kept beside OUTPUT (OUTPUT-decisions.json) and read again on a second run.\n",
